      "side": 1,
      "message": "patch_pkvm() is called twice: in apply_retpolines() and apply_returns(), for the same address range. Seems redundant?\n\nAlso apply_retpolines() and apply_returns() are called not just for the kernel image but also for modules (in module_finalize()), and it seems we don\u0027t need patch_pkvm() there?\n\nSo maybe it\u0027s better to call patch_pkvm() just once, in alternative_instructions(), after calling apply_retpolines() + apply_returns()?",
